\f1\fs26 You\'92d think when Sarah celebrated, she\'91d celebrate in lavish fashion, high above the clouds of the Layer. As was her Airborne entitlement. Surely, she\'92d commission an events empresario, who\'92d ensure the drinks were fashionable, the finger-food risked no stains on lavish evening wear, the music acts were the hardest to book, and the views evoked gasps among even the most over-sated dandies of the most over-dandied salons. Even if Sarah found some delight in such excess, she\'92d draw the line at opening the purging booths. She\'92d have no A-list guests gorging on her catering till the sun came up.\
Instead, when Sarah celebrated she randomly selected a friend, and dragged them to a particular karaoke bar called 
\f2\i The Blue Shade
\f1\i0  in The Grotto quarter of The Pale, the seediest district in the seediest of regions, where not only angels feared tread, but most of the unfortunate Cloudborne as well. \
Sarah was running out of friends; none ever agreed to a second celebration. Low on options, this time she invited Johnny.\
Sarah savoured Johnny\'92s discomfort.\
\'93Seriously?\'94 Johnny was exasperated. \'93An ELVIS bar?\'94 Dread and hope (hope this was all a joke) competed and made a caricature of his face.\
\'93They prefer being called Elvi,\'94 Sarah corrected. \'93Show some respect.\'94\
Sarah ignored the waiting line of ducktail and pompadour haircuts, the leather jackets and the jumpsuits. She dismissed the protests of the clip-boarded hostess (phoenix jumpsuit in pinks and blues) and the muscle-corded bouncer (all leather), and promenaded inside, towing Johnny in her persuasive wake. His alternating expressions of horror and disgust made his thoughts easy-reading. He was dwelling on the skin peels, hair treatments, detox regimens, new clothes, new glasses, new liver, and possibly even the new teeth he feared he\'92d need after visiting such a place.\
Sarah didn\'92t care. She was, after all, invincible.\
